 "_batch3_startups_finding": "Ran top brokers (Jesse Zhang, Alex Ortiz, Biju Ashokan) against the browser_finds + lead startups (Suno, Oscilar, HappyRobot, Legora, TrueBuilt, Taste Labs, Pallet, Gradial, StackAI, Legion Health, Salient, 11x, ClassDojo, Rula, Arcadia, Playbook, Cashera, etc.). Result: essentially NO 2-hop paths \u2014 these companies are too small/early (<~50 employees) for brokers' networks to overlap. The only hit was Samsara (a large public company), via Alex Ortiz. Takeaway: 2-hop referral pathing pays off at mid/large companies; for the small startups, direct founder outreach (or AJ's own 1st-degree) is the better play.",
 "_batch4_new_finds_finding": "Ran top brokers (Alex, Jesse, Chantel, Kayvon, Cameron) vs the strongest NEW finds. ADOBE is strongly covered (Chantel Benson is a Director of PM there = direct path for the Firefly Growth PM role, plus 6 more Adobe people via Chantel/Alex). Mercury's new Head of Growth Marketing reuses the existing path (Nick Dellis via Kayvon). NO 2-hop paths found for the other new targets \u2014 consumer cos (Poshmark, Hinge, Maven Clinic, Justworks, Commure, Unite Us, Genius Sports, The Farmer's Dog) and small AI startups (Abacum, Inworld, Listen Labs, Lemurian, LYNA): brokers' networks don't reach them. Direct application / founder outreach is the better play there.",
